{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1431461-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-fairy-godmother-arts","id":1431461,"title":"Changeling The Dreaming C20 - Fairy Godmother / Arts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-08T05:54:16-08:00","id":1431461,"title":"Changeling The Dreaming C20 - Fairy Godmother / Arts","content":"With which arts in Changeling would it be possible to conjure cantrips that resemble the powers of Cinderella's fairy godmother?<br /> <br /> Turn rats into horses, pumpkin into a carriage, goose into a coachman, transforming the dress and conjuring the crystal shoe.<br /> Would it be possible to do something similar using the arts of Changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","name":"YueSidhe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T06:04:54-08:00","id":1431462,"title":"","content":"Metamorphosis in the Commoner's book is geared towards that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T06:11:17-08:00","id":1431463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1431461-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-fairy-godmother-arts?p=1431462#post1431462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metamorphosis in the Commoner's book is geared towards that</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it, and I was wondering if that still applies in C20. Because there are several arts from the second edition that do not appear in the C20.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","name":"YueSidhe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T06:50:44-08:00","id":1431466,"title":"","content":"Yeah Metamorphosis, you could probably use any types of art to be a Fairy godmother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T20:04:24-08:00","id":1431530,"title":"","content":"Metamorphosis is much more powerful in C20. Thought it does lack afew things. Making carrages out of pumpkins and turning animals into people... still it gets you most of the way there. Naming.. well Naming cheats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T09:28:55-08:00","id":1431693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1431461-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-fairy-godmother-arts?p=1431530#post1431530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metamorphosis is much more powerful in C20. Thought it does lack afew things. Making carrages out of pumpkins and turning animals into people... still it gets you most of the way there. Naming.. well Naming cheats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Primal 5 - Dance of the five kings, wouldn't you be able to turn a pumpkin into a carriage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","name":"YueSidhe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T20:31:06-08:00","id":1431909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YueSidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1431461-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-fairy-godmother-arts?p=1431693#post1431693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Primal 5 - Dance of the five kings, wouldn't you be able to turn a pumpkin into a carriage?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you have a sufficiently large Pumpkin to start.. maybe. I'm willing to accept all plants count under wood(and metal under earth) But I've had arguments there. You'd still need a very large pumpkin or a willingness to use many small pumpkins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T14:10:58-08:00","id":1432538,"title":"","content":"Is another possibility that these are all chimerical items, and that Cinderella and the others at the Ball were Enchanted for a period of time, and their transformation back into mundane items are a result of the Enchantment ending? One no longer saw a faerie mien, but mundane reality.<br /> <br /> I don't know the rules of Changeling very well, but that the effects wore off after a set time seemed to me more like the period of Enchantment ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T20:15:31-08:00","id":1432879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1431461-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-fairy-godmother-arts?p=1432538#post1432538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is another possibility that these are all chimerical items, and that Cinderella and the others at the Ball were Enchanted for a period of time, and their transformation back into mundane items are a result of the Enchantment ending? One no longer saw a faerie mien, but mundane reality.<br /> <br /> I don't know the rules of Changeling very well, but that the effects wore off after a set time seemed to me more like the period of Enchantment ended.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Many powers have a set duration &quot;Scene, 12 hours.. glamour days&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}